event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","item_id":"rs_0586328e8a7aae4e016acba0131efc8190b2ae1ebc24e2084b","output_index":0,"sequence_number":102,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Evaluating editing strategies**\n\nI'm considering if I need to find replacements for multiple repetitive elements by making edits. Should I use a script to generate unique entries? There are tools available to edit requirements and match old text. I wonder if I can replace whole small paired blocks with unique context or do global edits instead. It looks like I should avoid using local range variables. It makes sense to modify the projectLocation signature, ensuring each redirect is unique. I can also think about how to edit full repeated post sections effectively."}

event: response.reasoning_summary_part.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_part.done","item_id":"rs_0586328e8a7aae4e016acba0131efc8190b2ae1ebc24e2084b","output_index":0,"part":{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Evaluating editing strategies**\n\nI'm considering if I need to find replacements for multiple repetitive elements by making edits. Should I use a script to generate unique entries? There are tools available to edit requirements and match old text. I wonder if I can replace whole small paired blocks with unique context or do global edits instead. It looks like I should avoid using local range variables. It makes sense to modify the projectLocation signature, ensuring each redirect is unique. I can also think about how to edit full repeated post sections effectively."},"sequence_number":103,"summary_index":0}

